ows (Win8+) standalone x64 binary (recommended for **Windows**)\n334\t[yt-dlp_macos](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/yt-dlp_macos)|Universal MacOS (10.15+) standalone executable (recommended for **MacOS**)\n335\t\n336\t#### Alternatives\n337\t\n338\tFile|Description\n339\t:---|:---\n340\t[yt-dlp_linux](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/yt-dlp_linux)|Linux (glibc 2.17+) standalone x86_64 binary\n341\t[yt-dlp_linux.zip](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/yt-dlp_linux.zip)|Unpackaged Linux (glibc 2.17+) x86_64 executable (no auto-update)\n342\t[yt-dlp_linux_aarch64](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/yt-dlp_linux_aarch64)|Linux (glibc 2.17+) standalone aarch64 binary\n343\t[yt-dlp_linux_aarch64.zip](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/yt-dlp_linux_aarch64.zip)|Unpackaged Linux (glibc 2.17+) aarch64 executable (no auto-update)\n344\t[yt-dlp_linux_armv7l.zip](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/yt-dlp_linux_armv7l.zip)|Unpackaged Linux (glibc 2.31+) armv7l executable (no auto-update)\n345\t[yt-dlp_musllinux](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/yt-dlp_musllinux)|Linux (musl 1.2+) standalone x86_64 binary\n346\t[yt-dlp_musllinux.zip](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/yt-dlp_musllinux.zip)|Unpackaged Linux (musl 1.2+) x86_64 executable (no auto-update)\n347\t[yt-dlp_musllinux_aarch64](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/yt-dlp_musllinux_aarch64)|Linux (musl 1.2+) standalone aarch64 binary\n348\t[yt-dlp_musllinux_aarch64.zip](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/yt-dlp_musllinux_aarch64.zip)|Unpackaged Linux (musl 1.2+) aarch64 executable (no auto-update)\n349\t[yt-dlp_x86.exe](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/yt-dlp_x86.exe)|Windows (Win8+) standalone x86 (32-bit) binary\n350\t[yt-dlp_win_x86.zip](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/yt-dlp_win_x86.zip)|Unpackaged Windows (Win8+) x86 (32-bit) executable (no auto-update)\n351\t[yt-dlp_arm64.exe](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/yt-dlp_arm64.exe)|Windows (Win10+) standalone ARM64 binary\n352\t[yt-dlp_win_arm64.zip](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/yt-dlp_win_arm64.zip)|Unpackaged Windows (Win10+) ARM64 executable (no auto-update)\n353\t[yt-dlp_win.zip](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/yt-dlp_win.zip)|Unpackaged Windows (Win8+) x64 executable (no auto-update)\n354\t[yt-dlp_macos.zip](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/yt-dlp_macos.zip)|Unpackaged MacOS (10.15+) executable (no auto-update)\n355\t\n356\t#### Misc\n357\t\n358\tFile|Description\n359\t:---|:---\n360\t[yt-dlp.tar.gz](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/yt-dlp.tar.gz)|Source tarball\n361\t[SHA2-512SUMS](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/SHA2-512SUMS)|GNU-style SHA512 sums\n362\t[SHA2-512SUMS.sig](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/SHA2-512SUMS.sig)|GPG signature file for SHA512 sums\n363\t[SHA2-256SUMS](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/SHA2-256SUMS)|GNU-style SHA256 sums\n364\t[SHA2-256SUMS.sig](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/SHA2-256SUMS.sig)|GPG signature file for SHA256 sums\n365\t\n366\tThe public key that can be used to verify the GPG signatures is [available here](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/blob/master/public.key)\n367\tExample usage:\n368\t```\n369\tcurl -L https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/raw/master/public.key | gpg --import\n370\tgpg --verify SHA2-256SUMS.sig SHA2-256SUMS\n371\tgpg --verify SHA2-512SUMS.sig SHA2-512SUMS\n372\t```\n373\t\n374\t#### Licensing\n375\t\n376\tWhile yt-dlp is licensed under the [Unlicense](LICENSE), many of the release files contain code from other projects with different licenses.\n377\t\n378\tMost notably, the PyInstaller-bundled executables include GPLv3+ licensed code, and as such the combined work is licensed under [GPLv3+](https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html).\n379\t\n380\tThe zipimport Unix executable (`yt-dlp`) contains [ISC](https://github.com/meriyah/meriyah/blob/main/LICENSE.md) licensed code from [`meriyah`](https://github.com/meriyah/meriyah) and [MIT](https://github.com/davidbonnet/astring/blob/main/LICENSE) licensed code from [`astring`](https://github.com/davidbonnet/astring).\n381\t\n382\tSee [THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt](THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt) for more details.\n383\t\n384\tThe git repository, the source tarball (`yt-dlp.tar.gz`), the PyPI source distribution and the PyPI built distribution (wheel) only contain code licensed under the [Unlicense](LICENSE).\n385\t\n386\t<!-- MANPAGE: END EXCLUDED SECTION -->\n387\t\n388\t**Note**: The manpages, shell completion (autocomplete) files etc. are available inside the [source tarball](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/latest/download/yt-dlp.tar.gz)\n389\t\n390\t\n391\t## UPDATE\n392\tYou can use `yt-dlp -U` to update if you are using the [release binaries](#release-files)\n393\t\n394\tIf you [installed with pip](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/wiki/Installation#with-pip), simply re-run the same command that was used to install the program\n395\t\n396\tFor other third-party package managers, see [the wiki](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/wiki/Installation#third-party-package-managers) or refer to their documentation\n397\t\n398\t<a id=\"update-channels\"></a>\n399\t\n400\tThere are currently three release channels for binaries: `stable`, `nightly` and `master`.\n401\t\n402\t* `stable` is the default channel, which offers releases published on a (mostly) monthly schedule. While it is named `stable` due to many of its changes having been tested by users of the `nightly` or `master` release channels, the latest `stable` release is often \"stale\" and prone to external breakage (i.e. sites changing things on their end and breaking yt-dlp).\n403\t* The `nightly` channel offers releases that publish shortly before midnight UTC on any day that sees changes to the codebase. This channel serves as a snapshot of the project's development, and it is the **recommended channel for regular users** of yt-dlp. The `nightly` releases are available from [yt-dlp/yt-dlp-nightly-builds](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp-nightly-builds/releases) or as development releases of the `yt-dlp` PyPI package (which can be installed with pip's `--pre` flag).\n404\t* The `master` channel offers \"canary\" releases that publish after each push to the master branch. This channel will always provide the very latest fixes and features, but may be prone to bugs or regressions. The `master` releases are available from [yt-dlp/yt-dlp-master-builds](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp-master-builds/releases).\n405\t\n406\tWhen using `--update`/`-U`, a release binary will only update to its current channel.\n407\t`--update-to CHANNEL` can be used to switch to a different channel when a newer version is available. `--update-to [CHANNEL@]TAG` can also be used to upgrade or downgrade to specific tags from a channel.\n408\t\n409\tYou may also use `--update-to <repository>` (`<owner>/<repository>`) to update to a channel on a completely different repository. Be careful with what repository you are updating to though, there is no verification done for binaries from different repositories.\n410\t\n411\tExample usage:\n412\t\n413\t* `yt-dlp --update-to master` switch to the `master` channel and update to its latest release\n414\t* `yt-dlp --update-to stable@2023.07.06` upgrade/downgrade to release to `stable` channel tag `2023.07.06`\n415\t* `yt-dlp --update-to 2023.10.07` upgrade/downgrade to tag `2023.10.07` if it exists on the current channel\n416\t* `yt-dlp --update-to example/yt-dlp@2023.09.24` upgrade/downgrade to the release from the `example/yt-dlp` repository, tag `2023.09.24`\n417\t\n418\t**Important**: Any user experiencing an issue with the `stable` release should install or update to the `nightly` release before submitting a bug report:\n419\t```\n420\t# To update to nightly from stable executable/binary:\n421\tyt-dlp --update-to nightly\n422\t\n423\t# To install nightly with pip:\n424\tpython -m pip install -U --pre \"yt-dlp[default]\"\n425\t```\n426\t\n427\tWhen running a yt-dlp version that is older than 90 days, you will see a warning message suggesting to update to the latest version.\n428\tYou can suppress this warning by adding `--no-update` to your command or configuration file.\n429\t\n430\t## DEPENDENCIES\n431\tPython versions 3.10+ (CPython) and 3.11+ (PyPy) are supported. Other versions and implementations may or may not work correctly.\n432\t\n433\t<!-- Python 3.5+ uses VC++14 and it is already embedded in the binary created\n434\t<!x-- https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/download/details.aspx?id=26999 --x>\n435\tOn Windows, [Microsoft Visual C++ 2010 SP1 Redistributable Package (x86)](https://download.microsoft.com/download/1/6/5/165255E7-1014-4D0A-B094-B6A430A6BFFC/vcredist_x86.exe) is also necessary to run yt-dlp. You probably already have this, but if the executable throws an error due to missing `MSVCR100.dll` you need to install it manually.\n436\t-->\n437\t\n438\tWhile all the other dependencies are optional, `ffmpeg`, `ffprobe`, `yt-dlp-ejs` and a supported JavaScript runtime/engine are highly recommended\n439\t\n440\t### Strongly recommended\n441\t\n442\t* [**ffmpeg** and **ffprobe**](https://www.ffmpeg.org) - Required for [merging separate video and audio files](#format-selection), as well as for various [post-processing](#post-processing-options) tasks. License [depends on the build](https://www.ffmpeg.org/legal.html)\n443\t\n444\t    Since ffmpeg is such an important dependency, we provide our own builds at [yt-dlp/FFmpeg-Builds](https://github.com/yt-dlp/FFmpeg-Builds). In the past, patches were applied to these builds in order to fix common issues for yt-dlp users, but currently our builds are equivalent to upstream ffmpeg. See [the readme](https://github.com/yt-dlp/FFmpeg-Builds#patches-applied) for details\n445\t\n446\t    **Important**: What you need is ffmpeg *binary*, **NOT** [the Python package of the same name](https://pypi.org/project/ffmpeg)\n447\t\n448\t* [**yt-dlp-ejs**](https://github.com/yt-dlp/ejs) - Required for full YouTube support. Licensed under [Unlicense](https://github.com/yt-dlp/ejs/blob/main/LICENSE), bundles [MIT](https://github.com/davidbonnet/astring/blob/main/LICENSE) and [ISC](https://github.com/meriyah/meriyah/blob/main/LICENSE.md) components.\n449\t\n450\t    A JavaScript runtime/engine like [**deno**](https://deno.land) (recommended), [**node.js**](https://nodejs.org), [**bun**](https://bun.sh), or [**QuickJS**](https://bellard.org/quickjs/) is also required to run yt-dlp-ejs. See [the wiki](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/wiki/EJS).\n451\t\n452\t### Networking\n453\t* [**certifi**](https://github.com/certifi/python-certifi)\\* - Provides Mozilla's root certificate bundle. Licensed under [MPLv2](https://github.com/certifi/python-certifi/blob/master/LICENSE)\n454\t* [**brotli**](https://github.com/google/brotli)\\* or [**brotlicffi**](https://github.com/python-hyper/brotlicffi) - [Brotli](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brotli) content encoding support. Both licensed under MIT <sup>[1](https://github.com/google/brotli/blob/master/LICENSE) [2](https://github.com/python-hyper/brotlicffi/blob/master/LICENSE) </sup>\n455\t* [**websockets**](https://github.com/aaugustin/websockets)\\* - For downloading over websocket. Licensed under [BSD-3-Clause](https://github.com/aaugustin/websockets/blob/main/LICENSE)\n456\t* [**requests**](https://github.com/psf/requests)\\* - HTTP library. For HTTPS proxy and persistent connections support. Licensed under [Apache-2.0](https://github.com/psf/requests/blob/main/LICENSE)\n457\t\n458\t#### Impersonation\n459\t\n460\tThe following provide support for impersonating browser requests. This may be required for some sites that employ TLS fingerprinting.\n461\t\n462\t* [**curl_cffi**](https://github.com/lexiforest/curl_cffi) (recommended) - Python binding for [curl-impersonate](https://github.com/lexiforest/curl-impersonate). Provides impersonation targets for Chrome, Edge and Safari. Licensed under [MIT](https://github.com/lexiforest/curl_cffi/blob/main/LICENSE)\n463\t  * Can be installed with the `curl-cffi` extra, e.g. `pip install \"yt-dlp[default,curl-cffi]\"`\n464\t  * Currently included in most builds *except* `yt-dlp` (Unix zipimport binary) and `yt-dlp_x86` (Windows 32-bit)\n465\t\n466\t\n467\t### Metadata\n468\t\n469\t* [**mutagen**](https://github.com/quodlibet/mutagen)\\* - For `--embed-thumbnail` in certain formats. Licensed under [GPLv2+](https://github.com/quodlibet/mutagen/blob/master/COPYING)\n470\t* [**AtomicParsley**](https://github.com/wez/atomicparsley) - For `--embed-thumbnail` in `mp4`/`m4a` files when `mutagen`/`ffmpeg` cannot. Licensed under [GPLv2+](https://github.com/wez/atomicparsley/blob/master/COPYING)\n471\t* [**xattr**](https://github.com/xattr/xattr), [**pyxattr**](https://github.com/iustin/pyxattr) or [**setfattr**](http://savannah.nongnu.org/projects/attr) - For writing xattr metadata (`--xattrs`) on **Mac** and **BSD**. Licensed under [MIT](https://github.com/xattr/xattr/blob/master/LICENSE.txt), [LGPL2.1](https://github.com/iustin/pyxattr/blob/master/COPYING) and [GPLv2+](http://git.savannah.nongnu.org/cgit/attr.git/tree/doc/COPYING) respectively\n472\t\n473\t### Misc\n474\t\n475\t* [**pycryptodomex**](https://github.com/Legrandin/pycryptodome)\\* - For decrypting AES-128 HLS streams and various other data. Licensed under [BSD-2-Clause](https://github.com/Legrandin/pycryptodome/blob/master/LICENSE.rst)\n476\t* [**phantomjs**](https://github.com/ariya/phantomjs) - Used in some extractors where JavaScript needs to be run. No longer used for YouTube. To be deprecated in the near future. Licensed under [BSD-3-Clause](https://github.com/ariya/phantomjs/blob/master/LICENSE.BSD)\n477\t* [**secretstorage**](https://github.com/mitya57/secretstorage)\\* - For `--cookies-from-browser` to access the **Gnome** keyring while decrypting cookies of **Chromium**-based browsers on **Linux**. Licensed under [BSD-3-Clause](https://github.com/mitya57/secretstorage/blob/master/LICENSE)\n478\t* Any external downloader that you want to use with `--downloader`\n479\t\n480\t### Deprecated\n481\t\n482\t* [**rtmpdump**](http://rtmpdump.mplayerhq.hu) - For downloading `rtmp` streams. ffmpeg can be used instead with `--downloader ffmpeg`. Licensed under [GPLv2+](http://rtmpdump.mplayerhq.hu)\n483\t* [**mplayer**](http://mplayerhq.hu/design7/info.html) or [**mpv**](https://mpv.io) - For downloading `rstp`/`mms` streams. ffmpeg can be used instead with `--downloader ffmpeg`. Licensed under [GPLv2+](https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/blob/master/Copyright)\n484\t\n485\tTo use or redistribute the dependencies, you must agree to their respective licensing terms.\n486\t\n487\tThe standalone release binaries are built with the Python interpreter and the packages marked with **\\*** included.\n488\t\n489\tIf you do not have the necessary dependencies for a task you are attempting, yt-dlp will warn you. All the currently available dependencies are visible at the top of the `--verbose` output\n490\t\n491\t\n492\t## COMPILE\n493\t\n494\t### Standalone PyInstaller Builds\n495\tTo build the standalone executable, you must have Python and `pyinstaller` (plus any of yt-dlp's [optional dependencies](#dependencies) if needed). The executable will be built for the same CPU architecture as the Python used.\n496\t\n497\tYou can run the following commands:\n498\t\n499\t```\n500\tpython devscripts/install_deps.py --include-group pyinstaller\n501\tpython devscripts/make_lazy_extractors.py\n502\tpython -m bundle.pyinstaller\n503\t```\n504\t\n505\tOn some systems, you may need to use `py` or `python3` instead of `python`.\n506\t\n507\t`python -m bundle.pyinstaller` accepts any arguments that can be passed to `pyinstaller`, such as `--onefile/-F` or `--onedir/-D`, which is further [documented here](https://pyinstaller.org/en/stable/usage.html#what-to-generate).\n508\t\n509\t**Note**: Pyinstaller versions below 4.4 [do not support](https://github.com/pyinstaller/pyinstaller#requirements-and-tested-platforms) Python installed from the Windows store without using a virtual environment.\n510\t\n511\t**Important**: Running `pyinstaller` directly **instead of** using `python -m bundle.pyinstaller` is **not** officially supported. This may or may not work correctly.\n512\t\n513\t### Platform-independent Binary (UNIX)\n514\tYou will need the build tools `python` (3.10+), `zip`, `make` (GNU), `pandoc`\\* and `pytest`\\*.\n515\t\n516\tAfter installing these, simply run `make`.\n517\t\n518\tYou can also run `make yt-dlp` instead to compile only the binary without updating any of the additional files. (The build tools marked with **\\*** are not needed for this)\n519\t\n520\t### Related scripts\n521\t\n522\t* **`devscripts/install_deps.py`** - Install dependencies for yt-dlp.\n523\t* **`devscripts/update-version.py`** - Update the version number based on the current date.\n524\t* **`devscripts/set-variant.py`** - Set the build variant of the executable.\n525\t* **`devscripts/make_changelog.py`** - Create a markdown changelog using short commit messages and update `CONTRIBUTORS` file.\n526\t* **`devscripts/make_lazy_extractors.py`** - Create lazy extractors. Running this before building the binaries (any variant) will improve their startup performance. Set the environment variable `YTDLP_NO_LAZY_EXTRACTORS` to something nonempty to forcefully disable lazy extractor loading.\n527\t\n528\tNote: See their `--help` for more info.\n529\t\n530\t### Forking the project\n531\tIf you fork the project on GitHub, you can run your fork's [build workflow](.github/workflows/build.yml) to automatically build the selected version(s) as artifacts. Alternatively, you can run the [release workflow](.github/workflows/release.yml) or enable the [nightly workflow](.github/workflows/release-nightly.yml) to create full (pre-)releases.\n532\t\n533\t# USAGE AND OPTIONS\n534\t\n535\t<!-- MANPAGE: BEGIN EXCLUDED SECTION -->\n536\t    yt-dlp [OPTIONS] [--] URL [URL...]\n537\t\n538\tTip: Use `CTRL`+`F` (or `Command`+`F`)  to search by keywords\n539\t<!-- MANPAGE: END EXCLUDED SECTION -->\n540\t\n541\t<!-- Auto generated -->\n542\t## General Options:\n543\t    -h, --help                      Print this help text and exit\n544\t    --version                       Print program version and exit\n545\t    -U, --update                    Update this program to the latest version\n546\t    --no-update                     Do not check for updates (default)\n547\t    --update-to [CHANNEL]@[TAG]     Upgrade/downgrade to a specific version.\n548\t                                    CHANNEL can be a repository as well. CHANNEL\n549\t                                    and TAG default to \"stable\" and \"latest\"\n550\t                                    respectively if omitted; See \"UPDATE\" for\n551\t                                    details. Supported channels: stable,\n552\t                                    nightly, master\n553\t    -i, --ignore-errors             Ignore download and postprocessing errors.\n554\t                                    The download will be considered successful\n555\t                                    even if the postprocessing fails\n556\t    --no-abort-on-error             Continue with next video on download errors;\n557\t                                    e.g. to skip unavailable videos in a\n558\t                                    playlist (default)\n559\t    --abort-on-error                Abort downloading of further videos if an\n560\t                                    error occurs (Alias: --no-ignore-errors)\n561\t    --list-extractors               List all supported extractors and exit\n562\t    --extractor-descriptions        Output descriptions of all supported\n563\t                                    extractors and exit\n564\t    --use-extractors NAMES          Extractor names to use separated by commas.\n565\t                                    You can also use regexes, \"all\", \"default\"\n566\t                                    and \"end\" (end URL matching); e.g. --ies\n567\t                                    \"holodex.*,end,youtube\". Prefix the name\n568\t                                    with a \"-\" to exclude it, e.g. --ies\n569\t                                    default,-generic. Use --list-extractors for\n570\t                                    a list of extractor names. (Alias: --ies)\n571\t    --default-search PREFIX         Use this prefix for unqualified URLs. E.g.\n572\t                                    \"gvsearch2:python\" downloads two videos from\n573\t                                    google videos for the search term \"python\".\n574\t                                    Use the value \"auto\" to let yt-dlp guess\n575\t                                    (\"auto_warning\" to emit a warning when\n576\t                                    guessing). \"error\" just throws an error. The\n577\t                                    default value \"fixup_error\" repairs broken\n578\t                                    URLs, but emits an error if this is not\n579\t                                    possible instead of searching\n580\t    --ignore-config                 Don't load any more configuration files\n581\t                                    except those given to --config-locations.\n582\t                                    For backward compatibility, if this option\n583\t                                    is found inside the system configuration\n584\t                                    file, the user configuration is not loaded.\n585\t                                    (Alias: --no-config)\n586\t    --no-config-locations           Do not load any custom configuration files\n587\t                                    (default). When given inside a configuration\n588\t                                    file, ignore all previous --config-locations\n589\t                                    defined in the current file\n590\t    --config-locations PATH         Location of the main configuration file;\n591\t                                    either the path to the config or its\n592\t                                    containing directory (\"-\" for stdin). Can be\n593\t                                    used multiple times and inside other\n594\t                                    configuration files\n595\t    --plugin-dirs DIR               Path to an additional directory to search\n596\t                                    for plugins. This option can be used\n597\t                                    multiple times to add multiple directories.\n598\t                                    Use \"default\" to search the default plugin\n599\t                                    directories (default)\n600\t    --no-plugin-dirs                Clear plugin directories to search,\n601\t                                    including defaults and those provided by\n602\t                                    previous --plugin-dirs\n603\t    --js-runtimes RUNTIME[:PATH]    Additional JavaScript runtime to enable,\n604\t                                    with an optional location for the runtime\n605\t                                    (either the path to the binary or its\n606\t                                    containing directory). This option can be\n607\t                                    used multiple times to enable multiple\n608\t                                    runtimes. Supported runtimes are (in order\n609\t                                    of priority, from highest to lowest): deno,\n610\t                                    node, quickjs, bun. Only \"deno\" is enabled\n611\t                                    by default. The highest priority runtime\n612\t                                    that is both enabled and available will be\n613\t                                    used. In order to use a lower priority\n614\t                                    runtime when \"deno\" is available, --no-js-\n615\t                                    runtimes needs to be passed before enabling\n616\t                                    other runtimes\n617\t    --no-js-runtimes                Clear JavaScript runtimes to enable,\n618\t                                    including defaults and those provided by\n619\t                                    previous --js-runtimes\n620\t    --remote-components COMPONENT   Remote components to allow yt-dlp to fetch\n621\t                                    when required. This option is currently not\n622\t                                    needed if you are using an official\n623\t                                    executable or have the requisite version of\n624\t                                    the yt-dlp-ejs package installed. You can\n625\t                                    use this option multiple times to allow\n626\t                                    multiple components. Supported values:\n627\t                                    ejs:npm (external JavaScript components from\n628\t                                    npm), ejs:github (external JavaScript\n629\t                                    components from yt-dlp-ejs GitHub). By\n630\t                                    default, no remote components are allowed\n631\t    --no-remote-components          Disallow fetching of all remote components,\n632\t                                    including any previously allowed by\n633\t                                    --remote-components or defaults.\n634\t    --flat-playlist                 Do not extract a playlist's URL result\n635\t                                    entries; some entry metadata may be missing\n636\t                                    and downloading may be bypassed\n637\t    --no-flat-playlist              Fully extract the videos of a playlist\n638\t                                    (default)\n639\t    --live-from-start               Download livestreams from the start.\n640\t                                    Currently experimental and only supported\n641\t                                    for YouTube, Twitch, and TVer\n642\t    --no-live-from-start            Download livestreams from the current time\n643\t                                    (default)\n644\t    --wait-for-video MIN[-MAX]      Wait for scheduled streams to become\n645\t                                    available. Pass the minimum number of\n646\t                                    seconds (or range) to wait between retries\n647\t    --no-wait-for-video             Do not wait for scheduled streams (default)\n648\t    --mark-watched                  Mark videos watched (even with --simulate)\n649\t    --no-mark-watched               Do not mark videos watched (default)\n650\t    --color [STREAM:]POLICY         Whether to emit color codes in output,\n651\t                                    optionally prefixed by the STREAM (stdout or\n652\t                                    stderr) to apply the setting to. Can be one\n653\t                                    of \"always\", \"auto\" (default), \"never\", or\n654\t                                    \"no_color\" (use non color terminal\n655\t                                    sequences). Use \"auto-tty\" or \"no_color-tty\"\n656\t                                    to decide based on terminal support only.\n657\t                                    Can be used multiple times\n658\t    --compat-options OPTS           Options that can help keep compatibility\n659\t                                    with youtube-dl or youtube-dlc\n660\t                                    configurations by reverting some of the\n661\t                                    changes made in yt-dlp. See \"Differences in\n662\t                                    default behavior\" for details\n663\t    --alias ALIASES OPTIONS         Create aliases for an option string. Unless\n664\t                                    an alias starts with a dash \"-\", it is\n665\t                                    prefixed with \"--\". Arguments are parsed\n666\t                                    according to the Python string formatting\n667\t                                    mini-language. E.g. --alias get-audio,-X \"-S\n668\t                                    aext:{0},abr -x --audio-format {0}\" creates\n669\t                                    options \"--get-audio\" and \"-X\" that takes an\n670\t                                    argument (ARG0) and expands to \"-S\n671\t                                    aext:ARG0,abr -x --audio-format ARG0\". All\n672\t                                    defined aliases are listed in the --help\n673\t                                    output. Alias options can trigger more\n674\t                                    aliases; so be careful to avoid defining\n675\t                                    recursive options. As a safety measure, each\n676\t                                    alias may be triggered a maximum of 100\n677\t                                    times. This option can be used multiple times\n678\t    -t, --preset-alias PRESET       Applies a predefined set of options. e.g.\n679\t                                    --preset-alias mp3. The following presets\n680\t                                    are available: mp3, aac, mp4, mkv, sleep.\n681\t                                    See the \"Preset Aliases\" section at the end\n682\t                                    for more info. This option can be used\n683\t                                    multiple times\n684\t\n685\t## Network Options:\n686\t    --proxy URL                     Use the specified HTTP/HTTPS/SOCKS proxy. To\n687\t                                    enable SOCKS proxy, specify a proper scheme,\n688\t                                    e.g. socks5://user:pass@127.0.0.1:1080/.\n689\t                                    Pass in an empty string (--proxy \"\") for\n690\t                                    direct connection\n691\t    --socket-timeout SECONDS        Time to wait before giving up, in seconds\n692\t    --source-address IP             Client-side IP address to bind to\n693\t    --impersonate CLIENT[:OS]       Client to impersonate for requests. E.g.\n694\t                                    chrome, chrome-110, chrome:windows-10. Pass\n695\t                                    --impersonate=\"\" to impersonate any client.\n696\t                                    Note that forcing impersonation for all\n697\t                                    requests may have a detrimental impact on\n698\t                                    download speed and stability\n699\t    --list-impersonate-targets      List available clients to impersonate.\n700\t    -4, --force-ipv4                Make all connections via IPv4\n701\t    -6, --force-ipv6                Make all connections via IPv6\n702\t    --enable-file-urls              Enable file:// URLs. This is disabled by\n703\t                                    default for security reasons.\n704\t\n705\t## Geo-restriction:\n706\t    --geo-verification-proxy URL    Use this proxy to verify the IP address for\n707\t                                    some geo-restricted sites. The default proxy\n708\t                                    specified by --proxy (or none, if the option\n709\t                                    is not present) is used for the actual\n710\t                                    downloading\n711\t    --xff VALUE                     How to fake X-Forwarded-For HTTP header to\n712\t                                    try bypassing geographic restriction. One of\n713\t                                    \"default\" (only when known to be useful),\n714\t                                    \"never\", an IP block in CIDR notation, or a\n715\t                                    two-letter ISO 3166-2 country code\n716\t\n717\t## Video Selection:\n718\t    -I, --playlist-items ITEM_SPEC  Comma-separated playlist_index of the items\n719\t                                    to download. You can specify a range using\n720\t                                    \"[START]:[STOP][:STEP]\". For backward\n721\t                                    compatibility, START-STOP is also supported.\n722\t                                    Use negative indices to count from the right\n723\t                                    and negative STEP to download in reverse\n724\t                                    order. E.g. \"-I 1:3,7,-5::2\" used on a\n725\t                                    playlist of size 15 will download the items\n726\t                                    at index 1,2,3,7,11,13,15\n727\t    --min-filesize SIZE             Abort download if filesize is smaller than\n728\t                                    SIZE, e.g. 50k or 44.6M\n729\t    --max-filesize SIZE             Abort download if filesize is larger than\n730\t                                    SIZE, e.g. 50k or 44.6M\n731\t    --date DATE                     Download only videos uploaded on this date.\n732\t                                    The date can be \"YYYYMMDD\" or in the format\n733\t                                    [now|today|yesterday][-N[day|week|month|year]].\n734\t                                    E.g. \"--date today-2weeks\" downloads only\n735\t                                    videos uploaded on the same day two weeks ago\n736\t    --datebefore DATE               Download only videos uploaded on or before\n737\t                                    this date. The date formats accepted are the\n738\t                                    same as --date\n739\t    --dateafter DATE                Download only videos uploaded on or after\n740\t                                    this date. The date formats accepted are the\n741\t                                    same as --date\n742\t    --match-filters FILTER          Generic video filter. Any \"OUTPUT TEMPLATE\"\n743\t                                    field can be compared with a number or a\n744\t                                    string using the operators defined in\n745\t                                    \"Filtering Formats\". You can also simply\n746\t                                    specify a field to match if the field is\n747\t                                    present, use \"!field\" to check if the field\n748\t                                    is not present, and \"&\" to check multiple\n749\t                                    conditions. Use a \"\\\" to escape \"&\" or\n750\t                                    quotes if needed. If used multiple times,\n751\t                                    the filter matches if at least one of the\n752\t                                    conditions is met. E.g. --match-filters\n753\t                                    !is_live --match-filters \"like_count>?100 &\n754\t                                    description~='(?i)\\bcats \\& dogs\\b'\" matches\n755\t                                    only videos that are not live OR those that\n756\t                                    have a like count more than 100 (or the like\n757\t                                    field is not available) and also has a\n758\t                                    description that contains the phrase \"cats &\n759\t                                    dogs\" (caseless). Use \"--match-filters -\" to\n760\t                                    interactively ask whether to download each\n761\t                                    video\n762\t    --no-match-filters              Do not use any --match-filters (default)\n763\t    --break-match-filters FILTER    Same as \"--match-filters\" but stops the\n764\t                                    download process when a video is rejected\n765\t    --no-break-match-filters        Do not use any --break-match-filters (default)\n766\t    --no-playlist                   Download only the video, if the URL refers\n767\t                                    to a video and a playlist\n768\t    --yes-playlist                  Download the playlist, if the URL refers to\n769\t                                    a video and a playlist\n770\t    --age-limit YEARS               Download only videos suitable for the given\n771\t                                    age\n772\t    --download-archive FILE         Download only videos not listed in the\n773\t                                    archive file. Record the IDs of all\n774\t                                    downloaded videos in it\n775\t    --no-download-archive           Do not use archive file (default)\n776\t    --max-downloads NUMBER          Abort after downloading NUMBER files\n777\t    --break-on-existing             Stop the download process when encountering\n778\t                                    a file that is in the archive supplied with\n779\t                                    the --download-archive option\n780\t    --no-break-on-existing          Do not stop the download process when\n781\t                                    encountering a file that is in the archive\n782\t                                    (default)\n783\t    --break-per-input               Alters --max-downloads, --break-on-existing,\n784\t                                    --break-match-filters, and autonumber to\n785\t                                    reset per input URL\n786\t    --no-break-per-input            --break-on-existing and similar options\n787\t                                    terminates the entire download queue\n788\t    --skip-playl